<title>AUSTRALIA: AMP SAYS MERV PEACOCK IN CHARGE OF SHARE LISTING.</title>
<headline>AMP SAYS MERV PEACOCK IN CHARGE OF SHARE LISTING.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Mutual Provident Society (AMP) said investment executive Merv Peacock had been put in overall charge of AMP's demutualisation process.</p>
<p>A spokesman for AMP Investment said Peacock, who was the head of marketable securities, would report to chief financial officer Paul Batchelor.</p>
<p>AMP, the country's largest funds manager with assets of more than A$90 billion and a major life office, planned to list on the share market sometime from mid-1998.</p>
<p>It was expected to rank among the top 10 companies.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
